# Environment variables — TEMPLATE
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values there.
#
#   .env.local is gitignored. This file is committed.
#   Never put a real value in THIS file. Names only.
#
# On Vercel the same names go in Project Settings -> Environment Variables,
# not in a file. There is no .env.local on the server.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both of the NEXT_PUBLIC_ ones are safe in the browser by design. That is what
# the prefix means: Next.js compiles them into the JavaScript it sends to every
# visitor. Anything you would not print on a poster does not get that prefix.
#
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The service role key bypasses row-level security completely. A page holding
# this key can read every family's medical details and every payment record,
# regardless of what the policies say.
#
# It is server-side only. It never gets the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, never goes in
# a component that runs in the browser, and never appears in this repository,
# in SharePoint, or in a chat message. If it ever does, rotate it that day.
#
# Used in ONE place since 27 Oct 2026: lib/supabase/admin.js, for the daily
# automatic emails (lib/reminders/). Set it in Vercel only.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# The automatic emails (0138). CRON_SECRET is VERCEL's: Vercel Cron sends it
# as "Authorization: Bearer ..." to /api/cron/reminders/ (a different value
# from the Supabase function secret of the same name). REMINDERS_MODE: unset
# or "test" = only @luke14ministries.net addresses are emailed; "live" =
# everyone (at go-live, after the purge); "off" = the job does nothing.
# STAFF_SUMMARY_TO overrides where the Monday summary goes; SITE_URL the
# address the emails link to (defaults to the request's own).

CRON_SECRET=
REMINDERS_MODE=
STAFF_SUMMARY_TO=
SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (Phase 2 — test keys only until launch)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test keys start sk_test_. Live keys start sk_live_ and appear exactly once,
# at go-live, directly in Vercel's environment settings. A live key on a
# laptop is a live key that can leak.
#
# ONLY the secret key belongs to this project. Payments use Stripe's HOSTED
# Checkout: a server action calls checkout.sessions.create and returns
# session.url, and the browser is sent there. No Stripe code runs in the
# browser, so there is no publishable key to set.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY was listed here until 30 Aug 2026 and
#   nothing has ever read it. It is removed rather than left blank, because a
#   name in this file reads as a thing to fill in -- and at go-live somebody
#   would have pasted a live pk_ into Vercel, watched it do nothing, and had
#   no way to tell "unused" from "not working". Put it back only alongside
#   code that actually loads Stripe.js.

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# The two webhook secrets are NOT Vercel variables. The webhooks are Supabase
# Edge Functions, so their secrets are set with `supabase secrets set` (or in
# the dashboard under Edge Functions -> Secrets) and are listed here only so
# the full set is written down in one place:
#
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET          -> supabase/functions/stripe-webhook
#   STRIPE_REFUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET   -> supabase/functions/stripe-refund-webhook
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY      -> both of the above, plus admin-reset-mfa
#   RESEND_API_KEY, RECEIPT_FROM, GIFT_FROM -> the two webhook functions
#
# Test-mode endpoints do NOT carry over to live mode. At go-live BOTH
# endpoints are recreated in the Stripe live dashboard and BOTH new signing
# secrets are set here. A missed refund webhook fails silently -- Stripe
# reports 200 and the site shows nothing (migration 0054).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH served the site from a subfolder on GitHub Pages.
# Vercel serves from the root. Setting it here breaks every link and every
# image on the site, and it fails looking like a stylesheet problem rather
# than a configuration one. Leave it unset. It is listed only so nobody
# "helpfully" adds it back.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resend (transactional email — registration confirmations)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Created in the Resend dashboard (the ministry's account, under admin@).
# Server-side only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_. Without it the site still works;
# confirmation emails are skipped with a warning in the server log, and the
# registration itself is unaffected.

RESEND_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Turnstile — the bot check on signup, login, password reset
# and, since 30 Aug 2026, the contact form.
#
# BOTH keys belong here now, and that changed on 30 August. The SITE key is
# public by design (it ships to the browser, which is why it carries the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix). The SECRET key is server-only and is used by
# lib/turnstile.js.
#
# This block used to say the secret "does NOT go in this project at all",
# because it was pasted into the Supabase dashboard and Supabase did the
# verifying. That is still true of the three ACCOUNT forms: they call
# supabase.auth.* straight from the browser, so Supabase is the only place a
# check can actually gate anything. The CONTACT form posts to a server action
# of ours instead, and nothing downstream would verify a thing, so it checks
# the token itself. Same key pair in both places; Cloudflare does not mind who
# calls siteverify, and each form issues its own single-use token.
#
# If TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is missing, the contact form still works and the
# server log says loudly that the check is not running. That is deliberate
# — see the note at the top of lib/turnstile.js for why a family who cannot
# reach this ministry is the worse failure of the two.
#
# ⚠️ ORDER MATTERS, and getting it wrong locks everyone out:
#   1. Set this key in Vercel and deploy.
#   2. Check the widget renders on /account/signup/.
#   3. THEN enable captcha in Supabase (Auth -> Settings -> Bot and Abuse
#      Protection), choosing Turnstile and pasting the secret.
# Enabling Supabase first makes every auth endpoint demand a token that
# nothing is producing yet -- no logins, no signups, for anyone. To undo it,
# switch it off in the Supabase dashboard.
#
# Leaving this unset is fine: the widget does not render, no token is sent,
# and everything works as it did -- provided Supabase-side captcha is also off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
